# RTK - Rust Token Killer (Windsurf)

**Usage**: Token-optimized CLI proxy for shell commands.

## Rule

Always prefix shell commands with `rtk` to minimize token consumption.

Examples:

```bash
rtk git status
rtk git diff
rtk git log --oneline -10

rtk ls
rtk ls src
rtk ls frontend

rtk grep "signalEngine" src/
rtk grep "backtestEngine" src/
rtk grep "ORB" src/

rtk find . -name "*.js"
rtk find . -name "*.json"

rtk docker ps
rtk docker compose ps
rtk docker compose logs
rtk docker exec trading-ai bash
```

## Meta Commands

```bash
rtk gain              # Show token savings
rtk gain --history    # Command history with savings
rtk discover          # Find missed RTK opportunities
rtk proxy <cmd>       # Run raw (no filtering, for debugging)
```

## Why

RTK filters and compresses command output before it reaches the LLM context, saving 60-90% tokens on common operations.

Always use:

```bash
rtk <command>
```

instead of raw shell commands whenever possible.

